      "prompt": "A vector has initial point $P(-3, 5)$ and terminal point $Q(4, -2)$. Write the vector $\\vec{PQ}$ in component form, then find its magnitude.",
      "answer": "$\\vec{PQ} = \\langle 7, -7 \\rangle$, $\\lVert \\vec{PQ} \\rVert = 7\\sqrt{2}$",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Subtract terminal minus initial: $\\langle x_2 - x_1, y_2 - y_1 \\rangle = \\langle 4 - (-3), -2 - 5 \\rangle$",
          "$= \\langle 7, -7 \\rangle$",
          "Magnitude: $\\lVert \\vec{PQ} \\rVert = \\sqrt{7^2 + (-7)^2} = \\sqrt{49 + 49} = \\sqrt{98}$",
          "Simplify: $\\sqrt{98} = \\sqrt{49 \\cdot 2} = 7\\sqrt{2}$"
        ]
      }
